CLAUDE.md:22:2. **`worklog/worklog_yixun/master_experiment_tracker.md`** — the living per-experiment index: status, headline verdicts/numbers, key commits, what's in flight.
CLAUDE.md:24:4. **`worklog/worklog_yixun/HANDOFF.md`** — the handoff doc: **log ALL working memory** — every in-flight run (exact command, PID/task id, log path, wall-clock ETA, what to do when it finishes), current experiment state and next steps, pending approvals, environment/GPU state, and any gotchas a fresh session would need to resume losslessly.
CLAUDE.md:36:- Role split: the main session model (Fable 5.1) does high-level planning, analysis and review decisions only; ALL low-level implementation (Coder rounds, tests, scripts, worklog tooling, data wrangling, log parsing) runs in **Opus 5.5 (`claude-opus-5-5`) max-effort** subagents, i.e. every Agent call that writes or executes code passes `model: "opus"` and never inherits Fable (per Yixun 2026-11-02; supersedes Opus 5 of 2026-07-25 and Opus 4.8); **OpenAI Codex `gpt-5.6-sol` at xhigh reviews it** via `~/.local/bin/codex exec -s read-only … < /dev/null` (review saved as `<exp name>_codex_code_review.md`). If Codex is unavailable, the declared fallback reviewer is Claude Opus 5.5 at max effort — say so in the artifact by-line. `-s read-only` does **not** protect the environment (it once permitted a `pip install` into conda base), so every review prompt must explicitly forbid installing or modifying environments.
CLAUDE.md:38:- Develop commit-by-commit from base `0bd5da0`: commits generally < 200 changed code lines, one-or-more commits per experiment, SHAs logged in `commits_<exp name>.md`. Archive (don't destroy) superseded code under `worklog/worklog_yixun/archive_*`.
CLAUDE.md:49:**Shared machine, concurrent writers.** A second Claude session works this same repo and branch (`check-equivariance-necessity`) from another machine and pushes frequently — **always `git pull --rebase` before committing**, and never rewrite files another session owns. ⚠️ **Queued Slurm jobs bind to commits**: exp_11 training legs verify their `EXPECT_SHA` at start via the *content-scoped* gate in `fa_orbit_train.sbatch` (Codex-approved, `da7ee7f`) — record/worklog commits are safe while legs pend, but commits touching the training closure (`train.py`, `defaults.ini`, `src/`, `data/AR`, arm configs, the launcher + its helpers) still abort them fail-closed. Never revert that gate to HEAD-identity. On neuronic, sbatch has **no `SBATCH_EXCLUDE` env var** — node exclusion works only as an explicit `--exclude`/`EXCLUDE=` argument (screen submitter only; the training submitter has no exclusion path). ECC-flaky nodes (Aug 2026): neu301/303/305/306/317/319/322/332. On the A6000 box, Yixun also runs experiments from *sibling checkouts* (`~/codespace/exp-12-arms`, `exp-08-cylvit-pe-cnn`, `exp-09-cyl-dinov3-no-ssl`, `exp-10-cyl-distill`) whose jobs share those GPUs and use their own experiment numbering. **Before assuming any `train.py` process belongs to this worktree, check `readlink /proc/<pid>/cwd`; never kill or edit a run you did not launch.**
CLAUDE.md:51:## Install & environment
CLAUDE.md:54:conda create -n flac python=3.10 && conda activate flac
CLAUDE.md:55:pip install .
CLAUDE.md:130:### Dataset & metadata pipeline
CLAUDE.md:146:Cross-experiment results live in `worklog/worklog_yixun/model_comparison.md`, regenerated **only** by `worklog/worklog_yixun/gen_model_comparison.py` (rows are glob specs aggregated from raw per-seed metric JSONs; single-seed screens are structurally excluded). Per announcement 04, regenerate + commit + push on every model-results update.
CLAUDE.md:181:`--sync-batchnorm` (ini key `sync_batchnorm` in `defaults.ini`, default `false`) forwards to PL `Trainer(sync_batchnorm=True)`. Default off leaves the Trainer kwargs **byte-identical** to the pre-flag dict, so existing recipes are unaffected. It is multi-GPU-only: enabling it with `num_gpus < 2` is a **fail-closed `ValueError`** (Yixun mandate), not a silent no-op, and `val_args` may not smuggle the key past that guard. (Landed exp_07, commit `f362673`, TDD, 40 tests.)
CLAUDE.md:208:`~/codespace/cylindrical-dinov3` (GitHub `Yixun-Hu/cylindrical-dinov3`, **private**) — a standalone package building a **cylindrical azimuth-equivariant DINOv3 ViT** intended to replace FLAC's geometry backbone. Deliberately a *sibling*, not a FLAC subfolder: it is `pip install -e`'d into the same env so both the continued-SSL training scripts and FLAC import one copy (`from cylindrical_dinov3 import ...`), and weights move via `save_pretrained()`/`from_pretrained()`. Do **not** fork Transformers or edit the installed copy in site-packages.
CLAUDE.md:212:- `vanilla_dinov3/` — read-only vendored copy of `transformers==4.57.0` `dinov3_vit`, hash-verified against the pip RECORD; the diff baseline. **Port against it, not against Transformers `main`** — v4.57.0 stores blocks as `self.layer`, `main` renamed it to `self.model`.
CLAUDE.md:219:## exp_25 depth_canon (2026-10-23 → FULL DONE 2026-10-29 10:34 EDT; eval campaign at pin `d6ca307a`: phase 1 DONE 03:34 EDT Oct 30 (90/110; the 20 seen-split cells refused by design), phase 2 TRAJ DONE 20:07 EDT Oct 30 (120/120, failed 0); RESULTS committed 20:22 EDT on the branch (HEAD `18241c7d`): Tier 1 PASS, Tier 2 FAIL as registered, Tier 3 PASS — exact C4 invariance at a θ = 0 quality cost; MERGED into `localization-exp` 2026-10-31 as `08bb9323` (sidecars `97e2e9ac`); comparison-table regen possible only on neuronic — the 23 older rows are neuronic-only evidence; S-block A / probe A CONFIRMED 2026-11-02; table regen by Yixun on neuronic per `neuronic_table_regen_2026-11-02.md`) — worktree `~/codespace/exp-25-depth-canon`, branch `exp-25-depth-canon`
CLAUDE.md:221:Canonicalization baseline for OrbitRIR (deepest depth-panorama pixel rolled to the left edge before every model input; invariance = shifted eval panoramas canonicalize to the same image). Bookkeeping in `worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/` (plan v15, notebook, ledger, Codex artifacts). Launch kit: `depth_canon_launch.sh` (gates: HEAD pin, 48-file pin manifest, config contract, tie audit, NAS, GPU memory floor 12 GiB per card with `shared` occupancy and co-tenants disclosed, W&B identity, pinned `WANDB_MODE=offline`, SMOKE projection cap 300 h) armed by `depth_canon_autolaunch.sh` (GO token → 3 clean polls → SMOKE → FULL); guard suite `depth_canon_guardtests.sh` (227 cases, `GUARD_NAS_READONLY=1`). Traps learned: **never edit a bash script while it is executing** (bash reads by byte offset — the launcher and the watcher run for days); committed SMOKE evidence JSONs are FULL-gate candidates (guard fixtures clear them); the `flac` env's wandb 0.15.4 cannot create ONLINE runs against the current server (`upsert_run → server_settings_introspection` → None) — every `--logger wandb` run in `flac` must set `WANDB_MODE=offline`; sync afterwards with `~/.venvs/wandb-sync/bin/wandb sync <run dir>` (a separate venv with a current client, key read from `~/.bashrc`; Yixun 2026-11-02: never upgrade the pinned `flac` env); a shared A6000 next to a 100 %-utilization co-tenant runs the recipe 1.6–5× slower (6–19 s/step vs 3.9). Reviews by Codex (`depth_canon_codex_code_r*.md`); see `HANDOFF.md` for pids, ETDs and the campaign plan. **Campaign traps (2026-10-29):** the registered composition probe must be run AT the campaign pin on a clean tree (`depth_canon_collect.py::probe_reasons` binds `source_sha == pin`) — run it after the pin commit and keep its JSON untracked until the campaign ends; its pre-registered ε_cond bound 1e-5 FAILED at 8.12e-5 for a numerical reason (float32 rotation roundoff × `dist_embedder` frequencies up to 2^10; Tier 1 exact; quarter turns bit-exact) — the adjudication (report as registered vs a plan v16 re-calibration) is Yixun's and open; a `pgrep -f depth_canon_eval_run.sh` guard in the launching shell matches that shell itself — rely on the driver's flock. The AR seen split (`acousticroom_seeneval*.json`) carries ONE sub-threshold item (idx 1194, `Office/Office_idx_15/S009_R092_hybrid_IR.wav`, −60.77 dBmax vs the −60 dB `is_silence` cut in `src/data/dataset.py`) that `SampleDataset.__getitem__` silently replaces by a random item, so every exp_25 S-block (seen-split) cell is refused by the evaluator's positional assignment guard by design (the unseen split has none; every seen-split number produced in this repo before exp_25 silently contained one substituted item) — S-block handling is Yixun's open decision. **Table-regen trap (2026-10-31):** `model_comparison.md` has only ever been regenerated on neuronic (`/n/fs/gatrdp/codespace/FLAC`); 23 rows — the 10 `exp_14 Z` rows (raws never force-added), the 12 exp_11 rows (`exp11_validate_rows.py` re-hashes checkpoints that exist only there and refuses the absolute neuronic `ckpt_path` elsewhere) and the 62.5k K=8 screen file — resolve only there, so on the A6000 box the generator refuses rc 4 (row regression) then rc 3 (exp_11 both-K gate). Never retract them with the overrides without Yixun's explicit order; the exp_25 rows themselves resolve from git alone (`dump_check="receipt"`, `check_link=False`). After the merge, exp_25 records go to `localization-exp` in the main checkout.
CLAUDE.md:225:The P1 phase is CLOSED (Codex r9z7, 2026-08-29; `worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_22_loc_meshgrid_claude/loc_meshgrid_results.md`). R2 runs the two remaining registered arms (plan r2 after Codex REVISE; the registered estimand is the mean across rooms of within-room medians / success_raw@1.0, paired room deltas, shared bootstrap matrix, Holm over 4) (`weights/exp20/{BF,YAW}_40k.ckpt`, digests pinned in `src/localization/meshgrid_report.py::REGISTERED_CKPT_SHA256`) on the frozen mesh protocol; plan `plan_loc_meshgrid_r2_bf_yaw.md`. Traps a fresh session must know: (1) `meshgrid_engine.assert_cacheable` REFUSES `cond_method != "vanilla"` by design — the inherited plan §1.5 narrower cache split for the C4 frame average is not implemented yet (round R2-B); (2) `localize_meshgrid.py` (the full-pass driver) has no emit-then-run launch records — only the probe driver has them (round R2-A ports them); (3) `REGISTERED_PROTOCOL["cond_method"]` is the literal `"vanilla"` and the canonical wording names the P1 result — a BF report is refused until the registration is arm-aware (R2-A); (4) BF must be evaluated under `--cond-method fa_invariant --frame-avg-angles 0 90 180 270` and YAW under vanilla — the eval-protocol flag is part of the experiment; (5) the P1 pass took 74.5 h wall on both cards (cafe / rest15 shards, `--batch-rows 256 --source-chunk 16`); (6) GPU ordering set by Yixun: these eval-only arms take the cards first after his current jobs end (≈ Nov 6), before any exp_09 seeds — never touch his processes (`readlink /proc/<pid>/cwd`).
CLAUDE.md:227:**exp_22 R2 state + traps (2026-11-04 12:10 EST; live state in `HANDOFF.md`):** R2-A CLOSED (Codex rA-F1 SHIP); R2-B + rB-F1…rB-F6 CLOSED (Codex rB-F6 SHIP 09:47 EST; four non-blocking NITs recorded as known limitations); the whole branch PUSHED at `a5608a60`; Codex R2 FULL (the final integrative review) = SHIP 09:56 EST; MERGED into `localization-exp` on Nov 4 as `4576b56238d57ce5d572f82ac6fbbdc9545e3430` (stamp location = the sidecar, Yixun 2026-11-04) — that merge commit is the PIN for the command list. CPU-only test runs in a checkout that holds the real data fail 11 GPU-only real-stack tests (`test_loc_meshgrid_queries.py` ×4: the AGREE `torch.load` has no `map_location`; `test_eval_localization.py` ×7: flash-attention has no CPU kernel) — pre-existing, gated only on data presence; run them on a GPU. Yixun 2026-11-04 evening: GO pre-approved, conditional on a FREE card (no other compute process for 30 min) — (a) the 11 GPU-only tests, (b) the gates, (c) the BF probe vs the 150 h cap — via a free-card watcher (to be built + Codex-reviewed); then STOP and report; the YAW / BF passes need one more explicit go; exp_35's cells run first on GPU 1. 2026-11-05: the command list is REOPENED (Yixun) so its gates, probe and passes use the same reviewed no-flash backend as P1 (see the backend trap in the exp_35 section); the watcher must never pre-empt the exp_35 lane. Gotcha for the launch: run the command list from a worktree at the PIN (the merge commit) with the assets symlinked, and never commit in that checkout while gates or shards run (every line checks `HEAD = PIN`; a mixed-SHA resume is refused). Codex rB-F3 judged every production fix RESOLVED, so production code (`localize_meshgrid.py`, `src/localization/`) is FROZEN at `701926e5`; rB-F4…rB-F6 are tests-and-proof rounds on the delete-the-check mutation proof (rB-F6: a statement-complete inventory, 606 atoms / 0 unmapped, 1118/1118 caught; Codex SHIP). The proof tooling lives in the session scratchpad (`rbf5/`, `rbf6/`) and is embedded verbatim (prefix `#   `) in the committed proof logs — a fresh session recovers it from there. BF per-row ledger stamps live in a SIDECAR `fa_ledger_stamps/<room>/q<pos>.json` (an in-row field would need a whitelist entry in the protected `meshgrid_crossarm.py`; Codex: equivalent) — Yixun 2026-11-04: keep the sidecar (DECIDED; no in-row field). The authoritative GPU command list is the exp_22 worklog entry `2026-11-03T17:17:46-05:00` (merged into `localization-exp`). Plan amendments A1–A6 live in §9 of the plan. Gate modes of `localize_meshgrid.py` (all record-free diagnostics writing `<out-dir>/<gate>.json`; exit 0 only on PASS; tolerances are constants): `--cache-parity-check --expect-arm YAW` (GV), `--fa-split-parity-check` (G1, autocast off, bit-exact), fa `--cache-parity-check` (G2), `--fa-production-parity-check` (G3, fp32, hard 1e-3), `--fa-production-drift-measurement` (G3D, resolved fp16, verdict `measurement`, no tolerance), `--replay-check --replay-against <P1 merged run>` (G0, pinned probe report `8c5fd5e8…`, A6000-class only). `--probe-room` is refused for every gate; G3/G0 refuse unless all 16 registered probe queries are consumed; a PASS needs the registered arm identity and captured provenance (clean tracked tree, git SHA, host, CUDA UUID). The executed fa partition is call-derived, checked equal to the declared `fa_partition` before every row, kept OUT of `run_binding.json` (pairing compares every binding field), and recorded in `run_summary.json` + `fa_partition_ledger.json`. Canonical BF/YAW reports and the crossarm need `--retrieval-handoff` (pinned `1bf62c05…`). Any code change after a shard started = restart that shard at the new pin, never resume. The BF probe is judged by A5/A6 (`factor × GPU-h × 0.5145 ≤ 150 h`).
CLAUDE.md:232:Give OrbitRIR B-F (exp07_BF@40k; evaluated `--cond-method fa_invariant`) the exp_25 yaw-invariance evidence CANON has — the random-yaw R cells (eval seeds 42–46, K=1 / K=8), a T-dup determinism cell, the Tier 2 scored waveform dumps (REQUIRED) and the Tier 3 spread row computed exactly as `depth_canon_collect.py` does — and add off-orbit 135° / 225° cells for P1@40k, B-F and CANON (60 cells) for a new figure `analysis/yaw_robustness/generated/yaw_offorbit_metrics.{png,pdf}` (+ summary CSV; `plot_yaw_curves.py` extended; B-F labelled OrbitRIR). MINIMAL: reuse the exp_25 runner and collector, no training; reuse (never re-run) the exp_10 A6 cells and the exp_25 results (record the exp_10 vs exp_25 admissibility). Cells run as ONE co-tenant lane on GPU 1 next to Yixun's exp_30 training (never slow it more than his own table jobs did), ahead of the exp_22 GPU tests and gates; report the figure-cell ETA to Yixun before running those cells. Live state in `HANDOFF.md`. **Backend trap (found 2026-11-04):** `flash-attn 2.7.4.post1` was installed into `flac` on Nov 1 23:14 (for exp_30); `src/models/transformer.py` uses it whenever importable (else SDPA) — exp_22's P1 and exp_25 ran WITHOUT it (their logs print "flash_attn not installed"), exp_07 / exp_10 WITH it. Any run that must match those references needs a reviewed, committed, hash-bound no-flash mechanism and a record of the backend actually selected (`eval_localization.py`'s `flash_attn_available` uses `find_spec`, which an import shadow does not hide). Never uninstall it (Yixun's env).

